 :decision-rule
 {:total-reporting
  "Every F29+ frame is reported, including nulls, aborts, and frames later
   found degraded. A degraded frame is reported AND MARKED with the named
   defect. No frame is dropped."
  :per-frame-instrument-version
  "Each reported frame carries the futon3c revision and any repair shas landed
   since the previous frame, so that an effect which appears only after some
   repair is VISIBLE as such rather than pooled away."
  :unit-of-evidence
  "The frame. NOT the series -- pooling across a drifting instrument is what
   the continuous-repair condition forbids."
  :level-2b-read "Memories are load-bearing iff the ablation arm fails to solve
                  problems the memory arm closed, over the rule-fixed set."
  :level-3-read  "Capability iff a held-out problem presumed beyond independent
                  reach is closed with the store and not without it."}

